     Marvin's post was correct.  The expression used is
 min_depth =3D In_quest(&u.uz) ? dungons[u.uz.dnum].depth_start : 1;
and In_quest() is false for all levels of Vlad's Tower, so the
minimum depth is 1, which is level 1 of the main dungeon.

     It's easy to get an approximate confirmation in wizard mode.
^V followed by ?, pick Vlad's Tower from the menu (it was G for
me; I'm not sure offhand whether that might vary), ^W to obtain
a cursed scroll of teleportation, r to read it, then use * for
destination to override implicit teleport control.  Odds are
good that you'll end up somewhere in the main dungeon.  If not,
repeat to try again.

     In general, either monster behavior or non-wizard mode
behavior could end up being different, but in this particular
case neither of them are.  Giving a cursed scroll to Vlad,
provoking him into reading it, then tracking him down would
take a lot more effort.  But after the first two steps it would
be straightforward to see whether he's still on one of the three
tiny tower levels, and the odds are very high that he won't be.


